{
  "name": "Fisherman's Bastion",
  "_about": "THE FISHERMAN'S BASTION (Hal\u00e1szb\u00e1stya), Budapest (Schulek, 1895-1902): a neo-Romanesque lookout terrace in white limestone along Castle Hill's edge, in three walked levels -- the lower hall behind its long open arcade; the lower terrace on its roof behind battlements, reached by the grand double stair to a projecting landing; the upper gallery set back on it, an arcaded cloister walk, and on its roof the upper walk behind battlements, climbed by a flight at each end -- and seven towers along the terrace with open belvederes and steep tent caps (`domed-tower`), the tallest in the middle.",
